.TH REWIND 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
rewind \- reposition a Crunch stream at the beginning
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "void rewind(struct FILE* " stream ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR rewind ()
seeks to the beginning of the stream and clears its end-of-file and error
indicators. The indicators are cleared even if the seek fails.
.SH RETURN VALUE
No value is returned. A failed seek sets
.BR errno ,
for example to
.B ESPIPE
for a nonseekable stream. A null stream sets
.B errno
to
.BR EINVAL ;
null is not a valid C stream argument. Success leaves
.B errno
unchanged.
.SH NOTES
Only Crunch streams are supported; they are not C library
.B FILE
objects.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fseek (3crunch),
.BR ftell (3crunch),
.BR clearerr (3crunch)
